SECTION 6: KV Cache Size Calculator
============================================================

The KV cache stores past key and value projections for each request.
Its size determines how many concurrent requests can be in flight.

  kv_bytes = 2 × num_layers × num_heads × head_dim × max_seq_len × bytes_per_element

  Model            Layers   KV Heads   Max Seq    KV Cache / req       Batch 32
  ---------------- -------- ---------- ---------- -------------------- ---------------
  LLaMA-7B         32       32         4096             2048.0 MB      64.00 GB
  LLaMA-13B        40       40         4096             3200.0 MB     100.00 GB
  LLaMA-70B        80       64         4096            10240.0 MB     320.00 GB
  Mistral-7B       32       8          32768            4096.0 MB     128.00 GB

For LLaMA-70B at batch=32: KV cache alone needs ~32+ GB.
On an 80 GB H100, that leaves ~48 GB for the 140 GB model weights —
meaning LLaMA-70B requires tensor parallelism across 2+ GPUs in production.

